e old name and the path `create/skill.md` with `/create:sk-skill` and `create/sk-skill.md`, including the schema helper's comment example and the contract test's sample of `commandDefinitionRelPath`. The packet and its folder keep their names. Verify: `OLD` over the seven files prints nothing, `node --check` passes on the schema helper and `node --test .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs` reports `fail 0`.\n94: - [x] T008 [P] Lane A. Rename the bridge's hand-kept entry and the hook guide's Claude row (`$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json`, `HD`). In the compatibility entry, change `inventoryId` and `id` to `command-create-sk-skill` and the description and the two keywords to `/create:sk-skill` and `create:sk-skill`. In `HD`, rewrite the Claude Code row of the `Starting a surfaced command` table: the second cell reads `Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists` and the Basis cell reads ``The Skill tool lists names, not files. A command file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill, an open upstream bug, so no command file carries that name``. Verify: `jq empty` passes on the compatibility file, `OLD` over the two files prints nothing and `rg -c '33 of the 45' $HD` prints nothing.\n95: - [x] T009 [P] Lane A. Rename the command in the root docs, the agent definition and the runtime notes (`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `.skilled/agents/markdown.md`, `.claude/agents/markdown.md`, `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/checklists/command-authoring.md`, `.codex/SYNC.md`). Make the same three edits in `.skilled/agents/markdown.md` and its hand-kept copy `.claude/agents/markdown.md`. In the checklist, point the YAML-router example at `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`. In `.codex/SYNC.md`, make the stub example name `create/sk-skill.md` and `/create-sk-skill`. Verify: `OLD` over the six files prints nothing and `AMSC` prints `all comparable mirrors in sync`.\n96: - [x] T010 [P] Lane A. Point the corpus rows at the new name (`CORPUS`). For `cmd-create-skill-typed-01` and `sv-07`, check that each `split` is not `holdout`, then replace `/create:skill` with `/create:sk-skill` in `prompt` and set `expected_command` to `/create:sk-skill`. For `cmd-create-skill-plain-tune-01`, check that its `split` is `tune`, then set `expected_command` only. For the one holdout row, change only `expected_command`, with one scripted substitution that never reads or prints a prompt: `sed -i '' -E '/\"split\":\"holdout\"/ s#\"expected_command\":\"/create:skill\"#\"expected_command\":\"/create:sk-skill\"#' $CORPUS`, and report only the count, from `awk '/\"split\":\"holdout\"/ && /\"expected_command\":\"\\/create:sk-skill\"/ {n++} END {print n+0}' $CORPUS`. Row ids stay. Verify: the `awk` count prints 1, `rg -c '\"expected_command\":\"/create:skill\"' $CORPUS` prints nothing, `jq -c 'select(.expected_command == \"/create:sk-skill\") | [.split, .row_type]' $CORPUS | sort | uniq -c` prints the four pairs of `spec.md` section 2, every line parses with `jq -c . $CORPUS > /dev/null` and `G diff --numstat HEAD -- $CORPUS` prints `4`, `4` and the path.\n97: - [x] T011 [P] Lane B. Read a negated \"show up\" or \"appear\" as a strong doctor problem cue (`HO`, `HOT`, `HCT`). In the first alternative of `STRONG_PROBLEM_CUE`, inside the verb group and right after `converg\\\\w*`, add `|show(?:s|ing)? up|appear(?:s|ing)?`. In the comment above the two cue lists, add one sentence saying a tool or command that does not show up or appear is a wrong state, like one that is not registered or not found. In `HOT`, add `reads a tool that does not show up as a strong cue` with `the deploy button is not showing up after the update` and `my new agent isn't appearing in the picker` as `strong`, and `don't show line numbers in the diff` and `show me how the advisor ranks skills` as `null`. In `HCT`, add `offers the helper beside t